-- Hatching (Cinnabar, channelled rush). Hatching is the run of parallel strokes an engraver cuts to shade a
-- plate, and the glyph is that run: Ticks strokes every TickInterval in a box Range deep in front of the
-- caster's validated frame, each one slowing, the last launching and stunning (GlyphEffects.Hatching). The
-- server keeps the beat against its start, so the strokes land at 0, 0.34, 0.68 and 1.02 s and the last at
-- 1.36; each is drawn on its own beat, three hundredths after the Anticipation and Cast, within a frame.
--
